; Implementation library for [Expr].  It contains the raw AST and all
; operations; [lib/expr] is the only supported public façade.
;
; cppo with no [-D]: [eval.ml]'s [value] is written as identical copies on
; both sides of an [#if defined JS_BACKEND] conditional (tail-call conversion
; Stage 3), so this stanza must route through cppo to select the [#else]
; branch, exactly as [expr_internal_js]/[expr_internal_mel] route through it
; to select the [#if] branch with their own [-D]. Every other module here has
; no cppo directives, so cppo passes them through unchanged. See .ai/.

(library
 (name expr_internal)
 (libraries core err_trace fmt)
 (preprocess
  (action
   (run %{bin:cppo} %{input-file}))))
